{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.chuhai.edu.hk/en/page/jobs?id=b9f07df8-bc36-430a-91ea-b8f196e36f18#assistant-associate-full-professor-open-rank-application-for-faculties": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor {Open Rank Application for Faculties}",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor {Open Rank Application for Faculties}. Hong Kong Chu Hai College - A Legacy of 78 Years, A Vision for the Future Established in 1947, Hong Kong Chu Hai College has a distinguished history of 78 years of academic excellence and contributions to societal talent development. As we approach a pivotal moment in our journey towards achieving university status, we are embarking on the most ambitious chapter in our history, poised for a significant transformation and new heights of excellence. To support this transformative journey, we are launching a comprehensive recruitment campaign for open-rank academic positions across our three core Faculties and one Institute. We warmly invite passionate scholars committed to shaping the future of our esteemed institution to join us in this exciting and meaningful endeavour. Positions are available in, but not limited to, the following areas: l Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences - Chinese Literature, Journalism and Communication, and English l Faculty of Business - Business Administration, Accounting and Banking, and Finance l Faculty of Science and Engineering - Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Smart Construction, Urban Planning, and Architecture l Ng Teng Fong · Sino Group Belt and Road Research Institute - International Trade, Cross-cultural Communication, and Regional Studies Who We Are Looking For: · Excellent Educators : Passionate and dedicated teachers committed to inspiring and shaping the next generation of leaders through innovative learning and teaching practices and student engagement. We are also seeking educators who have solid experience in developing programs that meet the standards and requirements for accreditation by the HKCAAVQ. · Impactful Researchers : Accomplished scholars with a proven track record of research excellence, including high-impact publications in indexed journals and successful acquisition of research grants. We are seeking individuals capable of establishing and leading dynamic research programs that contribute to the advancement of knowledge and elevate our institution’s academic standing. Additionally, we welcome applications from young, ambitious PhD holders who can demonstrate strong research potential, innovative ideas, and a proactive approach to developing their scholarly careers. Qualifications and Requirements l A doctoral degree in a relevant field. l A proven record of, or demonstrable potential for, excellence in learning & teaching and research appropriate to the academic rank (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor). l A strong commitment to academic leadership, curriculum and program development, and active participation in institutional service. l The successful candidate with relevant experience may be considered for a concurrent appointment as Department Head or senior academic management position, reflecting leadership capabilities and a commitment to advancing the strategic goals of the institution. l Fresh PhD graduate is welcome. Application Procedure Please send your application to recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk with the subject line \"Open Rank Application - [Your Name] - [Desired Faculty]\"."
    },
    "https://www.chuhai.edu.hk/en/page/jobs?id=b9f07df8-bc36-430a-91ea-b8f196e36f18#head-department-of-civil-engineering": {
      "title": "Head, Department of Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Head, Department of Civil Engineering. Key Responsibilities An academic leader responsible to ensure the effective operation and sustainable development of the Department. He/ she will be reporting direct to the Dean of Faculty of Science and Engineering. His/ her key responsibilities are as follows: Provide leadership in the development of the Department to align with the College's Strategic Plan and benefit the community at large; Ascertain the Department's high-quality and innovation in teaching, research, scholarly activities and knowledge transfer; Secure external competitive research grants; Ensure the Department's effective operation in terms of human, financial and other resources; Undertake teaching at postgraduate and/ or undergraduate level; Conduct and assist sub-ordinates to conduct researches that lead to publications in reputable journals and results in promoting advancement in the field; Undertake such other duties as assigned by the Dean of Faculty or the Management level of the College from time to time. Skills and Qualifications A Doctoral level in Civil Engineering and/ or a closely-related field; Substantial experience in a relevant senior academic position, with relevant professional qualification(s) (e.g. HKIE, etc); Strong track record in knowledge, skills, research and scholarship in the area of Civil Engineering and/ or a closely-related field, with a preferred focus on smart/digital construction, sustainable/resilient infrastructure, decarbonization, or ESG; Records as principal investigators for external competitive research grants; Good understanding of global trends in sustainability and smart transformation in engineering; Good understanding of and experience in local, regional and international higher education environment; Good interpersonal communication and effective resources management skills, with the ability to lead interdisciplinary initiatives; Good networks in both academic and professional bodies at local, regional and international levels. Application Applicants are invited to send their detailed curriculum vitae, including current and expected salary, and direct any enquiries to the Human Resources Office, Hong Kong Chu Hai College [E-mail: recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk ], quoting the position being applied for and the reference number. Recruitment will continue until the position is filled. Candidature may be obtained by nominations. The College reserves the right to make an appointment by invitation or not to fill this post."
    },
    "https://www.chuhai.edu.hk/en/page/jobs?id=b9f07df8-bc36-430a-91ea-b8f196e36f18#dean-faculty-of-business": {
      "title": "Dean, Faculty of Business",
      "description": "Dean, Faculty of Business. Chu Hai College has provided 78 years of quality education and excellence to the Hong Kong community and remains committed to enhancing educational opportunities for young people. Its purpose and vision are to nurture future leaders, strengthen the competitiveness of Hong Kong, and help bring about a stable, prosperous and harmonious society in a knowledge-based economy. Academic departments within the College include Chinese Literature, English, Journalism and Communication, Business Administration, Accounting and Banking, Finance, Computer Science, Civil Engineering, and Architecture. The Faculty of Business comprises three departments, offering programmes to meet the needs for both hard and soft skills in the business world, and to strengthen the ethical sense of our future business leaders. The College is registered as an Approved Post Secondary College under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320), with all degree programmes accredited by the Hong Kong Council for Accreditation of Academic and Vocational Qualifications (HKCAAVQ). The Dean of Faculty of Business is responsible for providing overall effective leadership in the management and development of the Faculty, the development of appropriate programmes in response to community needs, the smooth operation of programmes, the conduct of good quality teaching and learning activities, the promotion of research and scholarship and the establishment of partnerships with various external stakeholders in the Government, the academic profession and the industry. REQUIREMENTS The ideal candidate is expected to possess: 1. a Doctoral degree or equivalent; 2. proficiency in Chinese and English; 3. a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching, research and service commensurate with that of an associate professor, in disciplines of Business; 4. experience in serving in prestigious higher education institution(s) preferably at the rank of Faculty/ School Dean or above level; 5. abundant experience in providing effective leadership to Faculties or academic units with regard to disciplines of Business, including overseeing the development of academic strategy and its implementation; academic budget planning and allocation; personnel management; grants submission processes and management; and student enrollment MAJOR DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES The Dean, Faculty of Business shall: 1. be responsible for the management of the Faculty of Business and shall exercise the responsibilities of Faculty Dean in accordance as required. 2. provide visionary leadership and direction for the Faculty of Business, including formulating annual development plans and budget for the Faculty in accordance with the College practices. 3. lead the curriculum development as well as initiation and development of new undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in line with the College's Vision and Missions and Strategic Plan. 4. encourage high standards of teaching, foster and encourage research within the Faculty of Business. 5. establish and maintain connections with other academic institutions, professional bodies and industry, both local and international. 6. oversee staff management and accountability in the Faculty of Business. APPLICATION Applicants are invited to send their detailed curriculum vitae, including current and expected salary, and direct any enquiries to the Human Resources Office, Hong Kong Chu Hai College [E-mail: recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk ], quoting the position being applied for and the reference number. Recruitment will continue until the position is filled. Candidature may be obtained by nominations. The College reserves the right to make an appointment by invitation or not to fill this post."
    },
    "https://www.chuhai.edu.hk/en/page/jobs?id=b9f07df8-bc36-430a-91ea-b8f196e36f18#lecturer-department-of-chinese-literature": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Department of Chinese Literature",
      "description": "Lecturer, Department of Chinese Literature. Responsibilities Undertake teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; Undertake duties in course/ programme/ curriculum review and development; Perform academic and administrative duties; and Perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his delegate. Requirements PhD in linguistics, applied linguistics, Chinese studies or a related field but preference will be given to candidates with background in linguistics or applied linguistics; Specialty in second language acquisition / theoretical linguistics / sociolinguistics; Having attained level 1-B or above in Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi (PSC), or holding Certificate of Qualified Provincial (or above) Examiner for PSC; Preference will be given to those with capacity for English-assisted teaching; Capacity to teach the following courses: a. Second Language Acquisition, b. Language Policy and Language use, c. Design of Courses and Textbooks / Information Technology and Chinese Language Teaching, d. Topics in SLA and Teaching Chinese, and e. Chinese Literature- or History-related courses."
    }
